{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima and The Sickness feel like natural next choices because my recent listens to 10.000 Days and Ten Thousand Fists left me wanting to explore more Tool and Disturbed.",
    "City of Evil connects with the energetic riffs and melodic guitar work I enjoy in Advance And Vanquish, while Iowa fits the heavier intensity of my In Flames and Dimmu Borgir listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger's heaviness alone does not make it a match: its raw, repetitive approach is less appealing to me than music with melodic detail or intricate rhythms.",
    "I cannot connect Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 to my interests without knowing the artist or songs. Fallen fits part of my taste, but its melodic heaviness is less compelling than the more aggressive music I want today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat heavy music as broadly interchangeable, although forceful vocals, melodic guitar work, and rhythmic complexity appeal to me for different reasons.",
    "My earlier interest in accessible heavy hooks seems to carry too much weight today: Meteora and Hybrid Theory appeal, but I would choose more Tool and Disturbed first."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest listening makes exploring more Tool and Disturbed especially compelling, beyond a general interest in heavy rock.",
    "I distinguish between something I might enjoy eventually and something I want now; several albums fit my taste without giving me a strong enough reason to choose them on this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy music, but only some capture my current pull toward Tool's intricate songs, Disturbed's grooves, and aggressive music with melodic detail."
}"}
